    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does Teamwork Commerce prevent overselling limited luxury collections?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>RFID-verified inventory holds 99.9% accuracy in stores and warehouses worldwide. Each unit is individually tracked by EPC. If only 3 units of a piece remain (one in Paris, one in London, one in Milan) the system knows exactly where they are and prevents any channel from selling a ghost unit. For small production runs where a canceled order means losing a high-value client, this precision is essential.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does Teamwork Commerce track individual jewelry pieces?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Every piece is serialized as its own unit, with or without RFID. With RFID, the piece carries an EPC encoded as an SGTIN, a GS1 serial number that belongs to that one piece; without RFID, it carries its own unit ID. With RFID, a handheld counts a display case without handling a piece.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does cash work without a cash wrap?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Each associate sells from their own iPhone or iPad, so there is no cash wrap on the floor. Normally every POS needs its own cash drawer. Here, every device posts its cash in and out to one centralized drawer record, and the physical drawer stays back of house, so every cash movement across every device is tracked in one place.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Can Teamwork handle deposits, layaway and special orders?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. The platform supports deposits for custom and special orders and layaway, with automatic balance tracking and customer notifications. Custom pieces such as wedding bands start as review orders, tracked from the client's request to collection.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
